{
  "rules": [
    "Systematic underprediction in rising regimes: when the recent 10–15d trend is up, add an upward bias to the whole path (model is ~1–3 EUR too low across much of the horizon).",
    "Lag/slow reaction to breakouts: after an upside jump in the last few days, the forecast path catches up too slowly; shift the first 1–10 forecast days upward more aggressively than later days.",
    "Excessive mean reversion after strength: model tends to fade rallies and project pullbacks that do not materialize; dampen negative day-to-day changes when spot is above its 20–30d average.",
    "Late-horizon drift error: beyond ~day 20 the model often diverges downward (and sometimes adds noisy spikes); anchor long-horizon levels closer to the prevailing trend/level rather than reverting.",
    "Volatility underestimation around peaks: true outcomes show higher sustained levels after peaks; reduce the tendency to cap prices near recent highs and allow higher plateau formation."
  ]
}
